    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0818" n="808" xml:id="pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/18</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the
                        Division of European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Matthews</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">3629/19/43</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-09">December 9,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Matthews</hi>: I send you herewith an extract
                    from a telegram from the Foreign Office<anchor n="23" xml:id="d718-f1"/> about
                    staff for the Advisory Commission for Europe.</p>
                <p>It would be helpful to us to learn whether the United States Government
                    contemplates providing any clerical or typing staff, or any interpreters or
                    translators, for the Secretariat. Would you let me know your thought on
                    this?</p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Michael Wright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
